course: dictionary
lesson: 14950
title: Words that come back to life
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Some words are made from smaller parts you already know. Re- means again, and kindle means to set something alight. So rekindle means to light again. «The campers used one spark to rekindle the fire.» The fire had gone out, and they made it burn again.
explain: The same word can also describe feelings. «After twenty years apart, the two old friends decided to rekindle their friendship.» The friendship had faded, like a dying fire, and now it comes back to life. «Her kind letter rekindled my hope.» My hope had gone quiet, and now it burned brightly again.
explain: To check your meaning, swap in a simpler phrase such as «light again» or «bring back». If the sentence still makes sense, you have got it. Rekindle is a slightly formal word, so you will meet it most often in stories and books.
fact: Rekindle means to light again, or to make something burn strongly again.
fact: Rekindle can also mean to bring a feeling, friendship or interest back after it has faded.
fact: «Rekindle a friendship» means to make an old friendship start again.
fact: «Rekindle hope» means to make hope come back.
fact: Rekindles, rekindled and rekindling show the word changing for time: now, in the past, and while it is still happening.
exercise: «The firefighters tried to rekindle the dying flames.» What does rekindle mean here? | Put out for good | *Light again | Cook a meal | Wash with water
exercise: «The two old friends decided to rekindle their friendship after twenty years.» What does rekindle mean? | Forget it completely | Break it into pieces | *Make it start again | Write a letter to the school
exercise: In «She wanted to rekindle her interest in drawing», which word could replace rekindle? | Forget | Hide | *Revive | Lose
test: «The campers used one match to rekindle the fire.» Rekindle here means what? | Wash the pots | *Light again | Paint a picture | Build a tent
test: «His kind words rekindled my hope.» What does this sentence show? | Hope was in a box | Hope was lost forever | His words were rude | *Hope came back
exam: «After the long winter, the old songs began to rekindle joy in the village.» Which word is closest in meaning to rekindle? | Destroy | *Revive | Forget | Hide
